Z||000000||My7Fieros||06-08-2000||03:51 AM||||has anyone ever seen there forward exhaust manifold glow a brilliant red like Darth Vaders lightsaber? Well, I have, and its not something I ever want to see again! Water pump went bad (havnt changed it yet), replaced ignition module...car ran for about 3 or 4 minutes, manifold glowed bright enough to light Madison Square Garden, then died just as I was turning it off. Now wont recrank. Sounds good in starting (no odd noises I mean), but not getting a spark. Any idea? Also replaced coolant sensor (got a code15). Despite the "glow", I dont think (or hope) any real serious damage done. Prior to that, engine would only run for a few minutes, then die. Havnt checked for fuel pressure yet...any ideas would really help! Thanx!||||reg||11
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||06-08-2000||04:01 AM||||?<p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 06-08-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000002||bHooper||06-08-2000||06:49 AM||||after i got my car running agian, the manifolds glowed red hot.  however, my car was revving around 2500 RPM's.  <P>At that time the most common suggestions seemed to be Timeing, clogged manifold, or leaky injectors.<P>I might suggest you take a look at these options.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||lennyb4||06-08-2000||08:07 AM||||The first thing i would check would be for a clogged converter or muffler. I had this happen around two years ago. Turned out my cat was clogged.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroGT||06-08-2000||11:03 AM||||I know that one of the possible culprits for the glowing manifold syndrome is a bad EGR tube. This will create a lean condition and the aforementioned glowing. Check it out. <P><BR>John||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||06-08-2000||02:51 PM||||I really appreciate all the responses. Let me try to get a bit more indepth on the prob. Car was running fine, then water pump went and dumped the coolant. Then I got a code 15 (coolant sensor). Filled car w/ coolant, but didnt run engine while doing so. Also, EGR tube sh*t itself (does it ever end?). <BR>I replaced ignition module, then started car. Ran high RPMs (around 2100..due to EGR), manifold glowed, then died. Hmmm. (It has run for a few minutes and died a couple of times before this incident,thats why ignition mod.replaced). I replaced EGR tube, coolant sensor, and reset comp. Wont crank..dont seem to be getting spark. Batt was also super week..getting a new one today..could that be part of the no spark prob? More help would be great, and again thank you!||||reg||8
